# Two jobs: keep the secret out of the image, and keep ~1.6GB of build-time-only
# material out of it. Everything not listed here is sent to the daemon, so the
# exclusions below are what make `COPY work-a/ ...` mean "the pages", not "the
# pages and the OCR cache they were read with".

# The API key. Passed in at run time instead (docker-compose.yml env_file), because
# an image carrying a secret leaks it to anyone the image reaches.
.env

.git
.gitignore
.venv
.pytest_cache
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
**/.DS_Store
.claude/

# The source exam PDFs -- the ingestion pipeline's input, not the app's. The app
# only ever reads what build/ rendered out of them.
papers/

# Build-time only: the pipeline, its tests, and the prose about them.
build/
tests/
docs/
CLAUDE.md
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
.dockerignore

# The attempt log is runtime state and is mounted, not baked in. Baking it would
# put a child's practice history inside a shareable artefact, and freeze it at
# whatever it was on build day.
data/

# OCR caches. Build-time only, and ~5MB-plus per subject of no use to any route.
work/*/ocr
work/*/ocr-vision
work-a/*/ocr-vision
work-b/*/ocr
work-ans/*/ocr-vision
work-cn/*/ocr-vision
work/*/contact-sheet.png

# Answer-page renders, ~320MB of them. No route reads any of these -- the Science
# answers are served as text out of rubrics/ and the Chinese key is unpacked to its
# own directory precisely so that no URL reaches it (CLAUDE.md 7.1). Leaving them
# out of the image makes that structural rather than a matter of routing.
work-ans/*/pages
work-cn/*/answer-pages
work/*/answers
